sec.p:
Entrainment scores were calculated for open-loop fixed-frequency stimulations based on the power of the LFP spectrum at the target frequency during stimulus on (ptest) and stimulus off (pcontrol) intervals. [Full analysis func: Analysis/lfp_analysis/calculate_entrainment_score().]


E=ptest−pcontrolptest+pcontrol
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle E=\frac{p_{\text {test }}-p_{\text {control }}}{p_{\text {test }}+p_{\text {control }}}$$\end{document}

Suppression scores were calculated by first identifying the frequency with maximum power in the theta band (4 < f < 12 Hz) in the control power spectrum, then measuring power at that frequency in the control (ppeak_control) and test (ppeak_test) intervals. [Full analysis func: Analysis/lfp_analysis/calculate_suppression_score().]


S=ppeak_control−ppeak_testppeak_control+ppeak_test
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle S=\frac{p_{\text {peak_control }}-p_{\text {peak_test }}}{p_{\text {peak_control }}+p_{\text {peak_test }}}$$\end{document}

Outbound repeat sequences are defined as the number of visits to the same outer arm without visiting the alternate arm within an epoch. Note that these sequences are typically interleaved with rewarded visits to the center arm. We show the distribution of sequences of length greater than x in Figure 3E. This distribution under random choice of outer arm at each trial is given as
P(sequence>x)=1−∑i=1x(12)i. \begin{document}$$\displaystyle >x)=1-\sum_{i=1}^{x}\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{i}$$\end{document}
We sampled this random binomial choice process for the observed number of trials 1000 times for each animal group to get the 95% confidence interval of a random choice process in each case. Values for long repeat sequences below this interval indicate learning of the outbound task.

Entropy of the posterior distribution over discrete position bins is defined as:


S=−∑xp(x)log⁡[p(x)]
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle S=-\sum_{x} p(x) \log [p(x)]$$\end{document}
